e of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids shows October to November came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years, the most of any pair. In 2025 the middle of the grids got 26% of normal in January to February and 44% in November to December. Every grid had its driest year in 1955, with grid 25037 at 58% of normal that year. So far in 2026, February to March came in at 43% of normal on the middle of the grids.</p>"}
